{"summary":"The amendment fixes a real migration-contract violation: malformed schema-2 geometry/depth values are currently coerced into seemingly valid saves, which can silently corrupt dissolved totals instead of surfacing a SchemaMigration error.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-bc2dc25a","decision":"accept","rationale":"`migrate_v2_to_v3` currently clamps negative substrate depth, caps against possibly invalid fill height, and falls back to `scale = 0.0` when gross volume is non-positive. That behavior contradicts the documented migration requirement to fail explicitly on malformed legacy payloads, and it permits silent data loss during load. Rejecting invalid geometry/depth inputs up front and adding regression coverage next to the malformed-save tests is the safer and more maintainable behavior."}]}